On Wednesday 21 April 2004 21:30 Greg Sumner (gsumner@nwlinkNospam.com)
wrote:

> Death - Run away, he reduces your max hit points.  Rather quickly too.

Or zap him (her?) with magic missile-- not the wand, but the spell. The
higher level you are, the more damage it does. Death is rather wimpy;
brute force will work well. Don't *ever* use a wand of death or the
finger of death spell, it makes him stronger.

> Pestilance - Yes he makes you ill, keep a blessed unicorn horn handy
> and watch out if it gets cursed.

Unicorn horns aren't 100% reliable: have potions of extra/full healing
handy, or blessed tins of nurse meat if you're not human or don't care
about cannibalism, or the cure sickness spell at 0% failure. Pestilence
has killed more characters of mine on the Planes than all other causes
combined (still less than half a dozen, though).

> Famine - Makes you hungry yes.  I feed up before facing him and keep
> bite-sized food handy.

C- and K-rations are ideal. And/or stuff yourself on a dragon corpse or
something of similar size before facing him. Eat before you're weak,
preferably before you're hungry, or he'll have you fainting and
helpless.

> My general strategy is to lure them to one side of the plane and then
> maneuver yourself out of there so that they remain trapped inside
> whichever
> end you've put them.  If you're lucky a giant will be generated with
> boulders.  You can use a boulder to block a doorway.  They open locked
> doors so closing and locking doesn't work.

Note that scrolls of earth don't work on the Planes either. 

Pestilence and Famine react very well to wands of death and finger of
death spells, though if you're a high-level W (or conceivably P) magic
missiles work almost as well and take *much* less energy, which is
important when you're carrying the Amulet of Yendor.

> Also, use the insect swarms to your advantage.  At that point they
> should be
> harmless to you and keep the really nasty enemies at bay.  If you can,
> tame a whole swarm of monsters and summon them with a magic whistle to
> keep yourself surrounded.

You can teleport a swath through the ants, but watch out that you don't
hit any priests or peaceful angels (or Riders, who will be teleported
right to your side twelve times out of thirteen).

